## 4. What I could NOT check and why

- Full field novelty (all N-claims): no internet; fetch queues
  (7 quant + lexical + rate items) unexecuted. A documented null from
  those searches is the missing evidence. Sampling: read 3 lit maps +
  3 fetch queues + round-1 lit map fully; did not re-read every
  inventory file line-by-line (boundaries taken from the maps' own
  "already-scanned" lists, which I verified exist, not their contents).
- ITQ rerun with multiple inits / iter sweep: read-only mandate plus
  session cost; I recomputed from stored `RESULTS.json` only (sampled
  per-archive diagnostics shown, all 40 same pattern). No new fits.
- LME channel ablation (322/470 at publication) and LoCoMo gold: out
  of role scope; LoCoMo numbers excluded from all verdicts above.
- Clean-machine portability: already-known issue, not re-tested.

## 5. Safe-to-state list (how to hedge each)

- State as measured pipeline facts: RealTalk ITQ≤random on qscale with
  the exact protocol (1 init/50 iters/3+7 RANDs); k384 sign>float on
  RealTalk only; T3 scorer split; no-arm-wins-both in this system.
- State as exploratory correlations: size-damage r (n=10, Hit@10);
  balance co-occurrence (no causality); σ-whitening gloss (mechanism
  not isolated).
- State as internal nulls, never field claims: "no source in our
  scanned set" for ≤16B gold Hit@10 and few-hundred-doc regime.
- Cite for principle, not for instance: score-aware quantization for
  "reconstruction ≠ retrieval"; BEIR for "BM25 strong zero-shot";
  LSH/ANN framing for "first stage = recall device". Verify each from
  primary source first; the maps' UNVERIFIED tags must survive until then.
- Do not state publicly without new work: "ITQ fails on text codes"
  (needs multi-init + iter sweep + second pipeline), "balance hurts
  retrieval", "unstudied regime", "sign adds 10pp" (unscoped).

